{"id":"resp_abf89f44212f79e4","created_at":1795618587,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_923adee8e06b459e","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"The task: produce SHACL graph representing the requirement TRF-010 clause 1.8 about ice classes. Use ontology: iceClass property linking ship (benchmarkEntity subclass ship) to iceClassValue individuals (IA Super etc.). Need shapes to enforce that each ship has an iceClass value among those individuals? The requirement defines possible classes; we need to model enumeration constraint.\n\nWe must use exact canonical IRIs, property kinds, datatypes and units. Use quantityEncoding? Not needed as it's not quantity.\n\nWe have termOwners: iceClass belongs to ship. So shape target class ship.\n\nCreate a sh:NodeShape with sh:targetClass ship. Use sh:property with path iceClass, sh:in list of the six individuals.\n\nAlso note clause defines hierarchical order; not needed.\n\nInclude rdfs:label/comment from source.\n\nWe must not infer missing owners etc. We have owner already ship.\n\nThus produce SHACL.\n\nAlso need to include declarations for shapes etc.\n\nUse prefixes: sh, rdf, rdfs, nltl maybe.\n\nInclude the individuals IRIs.\n\nDefine shape: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ShipIceClassShape> maybe.\n\nUse sh:targetClass <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship>.\n\nsh:property: [ sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass> ; sh:in (list ...) ; sh:message \"Ice class must be one of IA Super, IA, IB, IC, II, III as defined in TRF-010 clause 1.8.\" ].\n\nAdd sh:severity sh:Violation.\n\nAdd comment referencing source.\n\nAlso need to include shapes for each valid value? Not needed.\n\nAdd rdfs:comment with source selection.\n\nNow produce final answer with <BEGIN_SHACL> line, then Turtle content, then <END_SHACL>.\n\nLet's craft.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_8642a3ab1382f346","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n\n# Shape that enforces the allowed ice‑class values defined in\n# TRF‑010 clause 1.8 (Ice classes) of the Ice Class Regulations\n# (2021 edition, file data/requirements/TRAFICOM_full.txt, SHA‑256 e0bf…e8ba).\n\nnltl:ShipIceClassShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    rdfs:comment \"\"\"\n    Requirement TRF‑010, clause 1.8:\n    “Under section 3 of the Act on the Ice Classes of Ships and Icebreaker Assistance (1121/2005),\n    ships are assigned to ice classes as follows:\n      1. ice class IA Super …\n      2. ice class IA …\n      3. ice class IB …\n      4. ice class IC …\n      5. ice class II …\n      6. ice class III …”\n    The shape requires every instance of nltl:ship to have an iceClass property whose\n    value is one of the six enumerated ice‑class concepts.\n    \"\"\" ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:iceClass ;\n        sh:in (\n            nltl:iceClassIaSuper\n            nltl:iceClassIa\n            nltl:iceClassIb\n            nltl:iceClassIc\n            nltl:iceClassIi\n            nltl:iceClassIii\n        ) ;\n        sh:message \"Ship must be assigned one of the ice‑class values defined in TRF‑010 clause 1.8 (IA Super, IA, IB, IC, II, III).\" ;\n        sh:severity sh:Violation ;\n    ] .\n\n# Enumeration individuals (exact IRIs as declared in the ontology)\n\nnltl:iceClassIaSuper a rdf:Resource, nltl:iceClassValue ;\n    rdfs:label \"IA Super\"@en .\n\nnltl:iceClassIa a rdf:Resource, nltl:iceClassValue ;\n    rdfs:label \"IA\"@en .\n\nnltl:iceClassIb a rdf:Resource, nltl:iceClassValue ;\n    rdfs:label \"IB\"@en .\n\nnltl:iceClassIc a rdf:Resource, nltl:iceClassValue ;\n    rdfs:label \"IC\"@en .\n\nnltl:iceClassIi a rdf:Resource, nltl:iceClassValue ;\n    rdfs:label \"II\"@en .\n\nnltl:iceClassIii a rdf:Resource, nltl:iceClassValue ;\n    rdfs:label \"III\"@en .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":35025,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":592,"cache_write_tokens":34432,"input_tokens_per_turn":[35025],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[592]},"output_tokens":1067,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":392,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1067],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":36092},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}